ret, wing pods, forward launchers, bombs): body-aim. If a seat other than the driver fires it, use free-aim instead, because that seat cannot turn the unit. Game code or data that places a weapon (a firing point on the turret) counts as the source saying how it is mounted; design trivia that ties the model to a real vehicle (a side gun based on a real helicopter's) does not. The family's default mount only fills in when the source says nothing about how the weapon is mounted and the body plan gives it no turret (5)."
